  "market_context": "Uptrend confirmed by higher highs and higher lows on AUD/USD 1H chart; price formed a consolidation zone, broke it downward (fake out), then returned inside the zone during London session.",
  "key_observation": "Price broke below consolidation (triggering shorts) but quickly reversed and closed back inside, confirming a fake out and bullish continuation signal.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified an established uptrend using higher highs and higher lows on the 1H chart.",
    "Step 2: Observed a consolidation area forming after an impulsive move up.",
    "Step 3: Noted price breaking downside out of consolidation — a fake out that trapped short sellers.",
    "Step 4: Waited for a candle to break and close back inside the consolidation zone as the long entry trigger.",
    "Step 5: Placed stop-loss below the fake-out low and set first target at 1:2 risk-to-reward, with second target via profit tracking."
  ],
  "outcome": "Long trade entered on close back into consolidation; first TP at 1:2 R:R achieved, second TP tracked with trailing stop.",
  "lessons": "Fake outs in strong trends offer high-probability entries when price re-enters the prior structure; always confirm with candle close and align with HTF trend bias.",
